<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Husain Arghun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1556</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah Husain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arghun">Arghun</a> was ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> from 1524 to 1556, son of Shah Beg, founder of the Arghun dynasty. He extended Arghun control over lower Sindh around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thatta">Thatta</a> and in the 1520s took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multan">Multan</a> from the Langah Sultanate. He opposed the fugitive Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humayun">Humayun</a> when he sought refuge in Sindh in the early 1540s.</p></div>
